<!--
Membership of placeholders that a type defines (#989), decided as for the placeholders an instance
declaration adds:
- AlphaType has the optional placeholder Item<no> of ItemType. Its pattern has a fixed part, so the name
  decides: Item1 (ItemType), Item2 (SubItemType, a subtype) and Item3 (BaseObjectType, a wrong type) are all
  instances of Item<no>, and Item3 is reported for its type.
- AlphaType has the mandatory, fully generic placeholder <Part> of PartType. Any name matches, so the type
  decides, subtypes included: PartB (SubPartType) is an instance and satisfies the mandatory placeholder;
  Other (BaseObjectType) is not an instance and keeps its own attribute hasOther; Item3 is not taken in.
-->

